      "title": "Go-to-market: ifm in data centers",
      "summary": "ifm presents AI data centers as industrial-scale liquid cooling plants that need monitoring to meet Tier III and IV uptime. It leads with process sensors, including dual-element temperature, pressure and flow, and with IO-Link for plug-and-work cooling equipment such as coolant distribution units and immersion tanks, plus HMIs with preloaded programs. Its message is faster commissioning and less overcooling, and it exhibits at Supercomputing 2026. Expect a Balluff rep to meet ifm at cooling-equipment builders standardizing on IO-Link.",
      "basis": "analysis",
      "fallback": true,
      "update_of": null,
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://www.ifm.com/us/en/news#strategy-profile-2026-11-11",
