      "title": "Go-to-market: Turck in RFID",
      "summary": "Turck sells RFID as tracking systems, not just readers. It leads with UHF read/write heads such as the Q150 (July 2026), which connect directly to Profinet, EtherNet/IP, Modbus TCP or EtherCAT, plus gate systems and a forklift system that reports asset moves to ERP or WMS. It targets production lines, intralogistics and automotive, and partners with label maker BSN for retail item tracking. Expect a Balluff rep to meet Turck where RFID data must reach both PLC and warehouse system.",
